 "class VCSCore usingPlatform: p vcs: vcs ide: ide = Object new (\n	(* A source control application that supports different VCS backends (git, hg, ...).\n\nSupport for new VCSs can be added by providing a custom implementation of AbstractBackend.\n\nCopyright (c) 2010-2011 Matthias Kleine\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining\na copy of this software and associated documentation files (the\n''Software''), to deal in the Software without restriction, including\nwithout limitation the rights to use, copy, modify, merge, publish,\ndistribute, sublicense, and/or sell copies of the Software, and to\npermit persons to whom the Software is furnished to do so, subject to\nthe following conditions:\n\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be\nincluded in all copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED ''AS IS'', WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND ...\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nWeb port — phase 1\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nOriginally written against Squeak: imports like `p squeak Set`,\n`p squeak ExternalLauncher`, `p squeak FileDirectory`,\n`p squeak CrLfFileStream` etc. Most of these were either (a)\ncollection types we now reach via `p collections`, or (b) the\nshell-out-to-the-VCS-CLI and filesystem support, which is concrete-\nbackend territory and won't translate to the browser at all (the\nreplacement is a forthcoming VCSIsomorphicGitBackendProvider).\n\nPhase-1 slot bindings:\n  - Set / List / Map  -> p collections equivalents (live)\n  - Stream / ExternalLauncher / Monitor / MultiByteBinaryOrTextStream\n    / CrLfFileStream / Transcript / FileDirectory -> nil. These\n    names are only sent messages inside backend or backend-adjacent\n    code paths (AbstractCommand.Launcher, AbstractLocalRepository's\n    repositoryDirectory, writeStream:toFileNamed:, the Logger's\n    commented-out body). Phase 1 doesn't exercise those paths;\n    when a concrete backend lands, it will provide them.\n\nLogger's `logMonitor = Monitor new.` slot is dropped — the only\nreference was a commented-out critical: section. log: is now a\nno-op (or routes through `out` if we wire it later). *)\n	\n	(* vcs is captured here so the lazy slots below — which need to\n   reach back into the sibling sub-modules vcs.sourceMirrors and\n   vcs.diffing — can do so at first-access time rather than at\n   VCSCore-instantiation time. The original Squeak code did these\n   accesses in the slot block, which only worked because Squeak's\n   simultaneous-slot machinery threaded futures through; primor-\n   dialsoup doesn't make that machinery available in this scope. *)\n	\n	|\n		private vcsHolder = vcs.\n		Set = p collections Set.\n		List = p collections List.\n		Map = p collections Map.\n		\n		(* Backend / FS / Squeak-only deps — unbound in the web port; concrete\n   backend modules will provide actual implementations. *)\n		Stream = nil.\n		ExternalLauncher = nil.\n		Monitor = nil.\n		MultiByteBinaryOrTextStream = nil.\n		private CrLfFileStream = nil.\n		Transcript = nil.\n		private FileDirectory = nil.\n		public logger = Logger new.\n	|\n)",
