 "public class SimulatedThread over: sim <Simulator> = Object new (\n		(* A suspended/steppable computation over one Simulator: the psoup Thread (MirrorsForPrimordialSoup) ported onto the JS simulator. States: #suspended (frames live, steppable), #broken (an unhandled signal; frames live at the raise point), #fulfilled (completed; result holds the value), #terminated. Where psoup's resume jumps to full speed via a primitive, resuming here runs the simulator to completion (psoup's resumeSlowly) - the only kind of resume compiled JS frames allow, and the right one for a debugging session. *)\n		\n		|\n			public state ::= #suspended.\n			public result\n			public simulator <Simulator> = sim.\n		|\n	)",
