 "addMenuClickListener: menuItem <MenuItem | Symbol> to: entry <Alien[HTMLElement]> = (\n		entry addEventListener: 'click'\n			action: [:event |\n				event stopPropagation.\n				currentHopscotchWindow activeMenuBlurred.\n				menuItem last value.\n				nil\n			]\n	)",
 "public awaitCoordinatedText: key <String> ifSuccess: sb <[:String | Object]> ifFailure: fb <[:String | Object]> = (\n		(* Wait for a coordinated TEXT result that some OTHER participant will\n	   produce under this key, without volunteering to produce it.\n\n	   The abstaining half of coordinatedText:via:ifSuccess:ifFailure:, for a\n	   caller that needs the answer but cannot obtain it here. The agent bus is\n	   the case in hand: an agent is a process listening on ONE participant's\n	   machine, so a client elsewhere can consume the reply but must not be\n	   elected to fetch it. Abstaining rather than declining keeps the election\n	   where it belongs - among the clients that can actually do the work - and\n	   costs no round trip to discover a client cannot.\n\n	   Here - a single, unsynchronized client - there is no other participant to\n	   wait for, so this fails at once rather than hanging. *)\n		\n		fb value: 'This exchange cannot be carried out from here, and this session has no other participant that could carry it out.'\n	)",
 "public backImage = (\n		^images backImage\n	)",
