 "lazyColumnOf: elements <Sequence> elementAt: elementBlock <[:Object | Fragment]> ^<LazyColumnComposer> = (\n			(* As above, over an existing sequence. The sequence is only sent #size and\n   #at:, so a lazily computed sequence never has to produce the elements the\n   viewport does not reach. *)\n			\n			^LazyColumnComposer count: elements size\n				elementAt: [:i <Integer> | elementBlock value: (elements at: i) ]\n		)",
 "lazyColumnOf: elements <Sequence> rowHeight: height <Integer> elementAt: elementBlock <[:Object | Fragment]> ^<LazyColumnComposer> = (\n			(* As above, over an existing sequence. *)\n			\n			| result = lazyColumnOf: elements elementAt: elementBlock. |\n			result assumeRowHeight: height.\n			^result\n		)",
 "lazyColumnOfSize: n <Integer> elementAt: elementBlock <[:Integer | Fragment]> ^<LazyColumnComposer> = (\n			(* A column that builds only the rows near the viewport. Takes a count and a\n   block from index to fragment rather than a list of fragments, because\n   materialising the list is itself linear in the length of the sequence and\n   would defeat the purpose. Use for sequences long enough that building every\n   row is the cost you are trying to avoid; #column: remains the right choice\n   for everything else. *)\n			\n			^LazyColumnComposer count: n elementAt: elementBlock\n		)",
 "lazyColumnOfSize: n <Integer> rowHeight: height <Integer> elementAt: elementBlock <[:Integer | Fragment]> ^<LazyColumnComposer> = (\n			(* As #lazyColumnOfSize:elementAt:, with the row height declared rather than\n   measured.\n\nPrefer this whenever the rows might not report a height on sight - editors,\nimages, anything awaited. Such a column cannot measure itself, and a column that\nnever measures never virtualizes: it stays at its bootstrap size, correct but\nnot doing the one thing it exists to do. Declaring the height at construction\nremoves that failure mode, where remembering to send #assumeRowHeight: afterwards\nmerely documents it. *)\n			\n			| result = lazyColumnOfSize: n elementAt: elementBlock. |\n			result assumeRowHeight: height.\n			^result\n		)",
